Please note: Debug.Assert is a method that writes an error message to the output window if the condition is false. If the condition is false at the time of execution, a dialog box appears saying "Assert failed". To use Debug.Assert, you should include the System.Diagnostics namespace in your project and call Debug.Assert before the code where the assertion occurs.--------------------The following is an assertion that checks if the result of the `Contains` method in `ArrayList.Test` is `true`, the index of `x` in `New_arrList` is not equal to the size of `Old_arrList`.

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == true, "If the return value is true, last position of x in new array is not the size of old array.");
```

This assertion checks that the condition `New_Ret == true` (the `Contains` method returned `true` for `x`) holds. If the condition is not met, the string `"If the return value is true, last position of x in new array is not the size of old array."` (which is the second argument of `Assert`) gets logged as a debug message.--------------------The output corresponding to the "@@@ If the return value is true, last position of x in new array is not the size of old array" comment would be the following csharp code:

```cs
Debug.Assert(!New_Ret || New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListCount);
```

This Assert statement will fail if the Contains method returns true (`New_Ret` is true), but the last index of `x` in the new array (`New_arrListLastIndexOfX`) is equal to the count of old array (`Old_arrListCount`). The statement means that if `x` is contained in the array (in the state after the method call), it must not be at the last position.--------------------```cs
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_ContainsContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
	    // @@@ The old array list count should be less than or equals to the initial count of the array list
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount <= arrList.Count);

	    // @@@ The old array list count should be equal to the expected count of the array list after 'Contains' operation
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);

	    // @@@ The indexes of x in the old array list should be lesser than the indexes in the new array 
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX);

	    // @@@ The last indexes of x in the old array list should be greater than or equals to the last indexes in the new array 
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

	    // @@@ If the return value is false, the count of x in the new array list should be either less than or equals to the old count of x
            if (!New_Ret)
            {
                Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);
            }

	    // @@@ If the return value is false, the indexes of x in the new array list should not be equal to the old indexes of x
            if (!New_Ret)
            {
                Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX != Old_arrListIndexOfX);
            }

	    // @@@ The indexes and last indexes of x in the old list and new list should be consistent with each other
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX && New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX && New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);

	    // @@@ If the return value is true, then the last index of x in the array should not equal to the array size
            if (New_Ret)
            {
                Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX != New_arrListCount);
            }

	    // More assertions can be added based on additional conditions
        }
    }
}
```

Note: This code assumes that the 'ArrayList' class has a 'Contains' method and 'IndexOf' and 'Count' properties as well as a 'LastIndexOf' method. Also PexObserve.ValueForViewing is used for viewing the values during debugging but in this case, I have used Debug.Assert for the same purpose. For a production level code, PexObserve.ValueForViewing should be used.--------------------